      "sourceTextSha256": "f9b3a571d4b8ea3adbd7bb40707a147d311cc052348a21cfc1a4e179eb9af2e8",
      "text": "Day 5 · Private transfer to the bus station and shared bus to El Calafate, then private transfer to your hotel.\n\nEl Calafate, on the shore of Lago Argentino, is the gateway to Los Glaciares National Park, which stretches some 170 km along the Chilean border. A UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1981, the park is about 40% covered by ice fields, with 47 major glaciers, 13 of which flow east to feed Lake Viedma and Lago Argentino, and some 190 smaller glaciers.",
